Z||000000||blue87SE||04-10-2001||11:52 AM||||Does anyone have any info on these cars? Like how rare they are and about how much it would be worth? It is in perfect condition and still has it's original blue paint that is in great condition.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Kelvin Vivian||04-10-2001||02:48 PM||||I have never seen a blue 87 SE, so if you could post some pics, that would be great...<BR>I do not know the color breakdown for each model Fiero. Of the blue cars I've seen, they have been GTs and coupes.<P>As far as 1987 Fiero colors go:<BR>White - 2,611<BR>Black - 8,402<BR>Silver - 6,671<BR>Medium Red Metallic - 20,264<BR>Blue - 4,458<BR>Gold - 4,119<P>As far as 1984-1988 Fiero colors go, the top 4 rare colors in order are:<BR>1) Yellow - 1,166 (all 88)<BR>2) Blue - 4,458 (all 87)<BR>3) Gold - 20,444 (16,325 86 + 4,119 87)<BR>4) Medium Red Metallic - 22,993 (20,264 87 + (2,729 88)<P>And as far as 1987 SEs go:<BR>There were 3875 SEs produced (2474 V6 + 1401 4-cyl)<P>Here's a pic of my 87 SE below...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402878&Sequence=3&res=high"> <BR>1987 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd Isuzu, AC, subwoofer/performance sound, spoiler, sunroof, manual windows, manual locks, manual mirrors, no cruise, no rear def, has GT grey rims and holley scoop added.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||04-10-2001||03:51 PM||||Hmmmmm.. Ive seen 87 Blue GT's & Coupe's, but never an SE..?<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A>||||reg||10
Z||000003||KEV||04-10-2001||04:16 PM||||in 87 the SE model had the smallest production numbers and they we're all areo nose notchbacks and came with either a tech 4 or the 2.8 V6, a blue one is the most rarest of the SE's. if you dodn't get it i'll take it. the production number was somewhere around 1,100 total +/- a couple hundred.  kev||||reg||1
Z||000004||JetroGT||04-10-2001||04:40 PM||||I've only seen one. And it was in need of some work. It was a 4cly 5spd. It looked just like any other SE, dual exhaust and everything.||||reg||14
Z||000005||blue87SE||04-10-2001||05:01 PM||||Here are some pictures of it....I think that is is in GREAT condition to be original paint and and original interior and body panels....and in the pic kinda looking over the car it is the sun and the clouds reflecting off the piant....it is not faded. It runs perfect and has 104000 miles on it and the last owner just put a clutch and egr tube and many other nicknacks on it and has tons of reciepts over the years of what has been done to the car... If anyone can tell me more about these I would really appreciate it, the guy at the Fiero Factory said he had only seen one other one too, and it has the 21 code for the blue paint so it is original and you can actually tell by the paint in the picture and tell that it is the gm color. On the inside that is a patch that the last owner put on to keep the seat from tearing from getting in and out. Thanks for the replies so far!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.southernfbody.com/fiero.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.southernfbody.com/fiero.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.southernfbody.com/blueseback.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.southernfbody.com/blueseback.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.southernfbody.com/blueseinside.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.southernfbody.com/blueseinside.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||blue87SE||04-10-2001||05:07 PM||||Oh yeah...it is a 2.8l v6 with a getrag 5 speed that is AWSOME this thing runs like a top, it has manual windows and door lock but has very cold ac but didn't have the sun roof....I was going to get a gt with everything but I really liked this blue se and I was told that it was rare. So now it is mine!! If anyone has any idea what it should be worth I would really appreciate it...I don't want to sell it but I just want to get an idea of how good a deal I got. I am pretty new to the fiero community but I have been wanting one for a long time....I have always loved pontiacs btw my other car is a 2000 trans-am, so I do know some but not alot.<P>Thanks alot for the help,<BR>Jeremy||||reg||1
Z||000007||Kelvin Vivian||04-10-2001||09:27 PM||||Jeremy here is your car...<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.southernfbody.com/fiero.jpg">     <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.southernfbody.com/blueseback.jpg">  <BR>Very nice... First blue SE I've seen. Not that you plan to sell it, but if you did sell it, a Fiero collector would appreciate it and would be willing to pay more than the average person. I like it A LOT.<P>In 1987, the gas tank was increased from 10.2 gal to 11.9 gal. The headlight motor assembly was upgraded. Your V6 has the 5-spd getrag. The V6 intake plenum has the engraved "Fiero". I say keep this car, but continue to keep your eyes on the lookout for a GT that you like, and then become a multiple Fiero owner...<p>[This message has been edited by Kelvin Vivian (edited 04-11-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000008||Cheever2||04-10-2001||09:41 PM||||We all share your enthusiasm, and wish you nothing but the best of times with your Fiero, but you really don't have to post the same thing on every section in the Forum.<P>I'll compare this to the 88 I got over a year ago, with 57000 miles, and it was a one-owner... I paid $3000.  Did you pay less than that?<BR>||||reg||1
